{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-everyday-australia-part-2/audio/main-a458a96c3c53.mp3","durationSec":341.328,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":4.12,"text":"Canberra is the capital of Australia, and it is a planned city."},{"start":5.02,"end":8.36,"text":"People drew the city on paper first, and then they built it."},{"start":8.98,"end":9.2,"text":"Why?"},{"start":10.3,"end":14.7,"text":"When Australia became one country, Sydney and Melbourne both wanted to be the capital."},{"start":15.16,"end":15.94,"text":"They could not agree."},{"start":16.24,"end":18.24,"text":"So the government built a new city between them."},{"start":18.72,"end":22.92,"text":"Two Americans, a husband and wife, won a competition to draw the new city."},{"start":23.58,"end":26.86,"text":"They were Walter Burley Griffin and Marion Mahony Griffin."},{"start":27.51,"end":30.68,"text":"For the Griffins, a lake was the heart of the city."},{"start":31.38,"end":31.96,"text":"Why a lake?"},{"start":32.44,"end":34.6,"text":"The river was in low land between hills."},{"start":35.2,"end":39.68,"text":"Water could fill this low land easily and cheaply, and a lake would be beautiful."},{"start":40.44,"end":42.94,"text":"So the Griffins drew the city around it."},{"start":43.26,"end":45.28,"text":"But Canberra had only a small river."},{"start":45.78,"end":49.32,"text":"So workers built a dam, a big wall that stops a river."},{"start":50.12,"end":52.48,"text":"In 1963, they closed its gates."},{"start":53.06,"end":56.8,"text":"The river water stopped at the wall, and slowly it made a lake."},{"start":57.36,"end":59.34,"text":"Its name is Lake Burley Griffin."},{"start":60.42,"end":62.54,"text":"Today the lake is the weekend park for the city."},{"start":63.06,"end":65.68,"text":"People walk or ride bikes on the bridge-to-bridge loop."},{"start":66,"end":67.66,"text":"It is a 5-kilometre circle."},{"start":68,"end":69.16,"text":"It goes over two bridges."},{"start":70.1,"end":73.22,"text":"Rowing clubs train in long, thin boats at the west end."},{"start":73.22,"end":78.12,"text":"Families cook lunch on the free electric barbecues by the water."},{"start":78.9,"end":83.12,"text":"A sausage sizzle is a barbecue that sells food to raise money for a group."},{"start":84.22,"end":87.06,"text":"Sizzle is the sound of food cooking on a hot plate."},{"start":87.06,"end":90.4,"text":"You get one sausage in a slice of white bread."},{"start":91.2,"end":93.8,"text":"Many people add fried onions and tomato sauce."},{"start":94.68,"end":98.98,"text":"The most famous ones are outside Bunnings, a big hardware shop."},{"start":100.12,"end":103.54,"text":"A hardware shop sells tools and things for your house and garden."},{"start":104.6,"end":109.32,"text":"On weekends, a local group, like a school or a sports club, cooks there."},{"start":110.08,"end":113.52,"text":"Bunnings takes no money from the group, so the group keeps it all."},{"start":113.52,"end":116.82,"text":"A sausage costs $3.50."},{"start":118.06,"end":121.96,"text":"Sausage sizzles also appear on election day, the day people vote."},{"start":122.42,"end":125.74,"text":"They are at polling places, the places where people vote."},{"start":126.64,"end":127.14,"text":"Why there?"},{"start":128.44,"end":130.54,"text":"In Australia, voting is compulsory."},{"start":131.5,"end":134.9,"text":"Every Australian citizen aged 18 or older must vote."},{"start":135.74,"end":138.02,"text":"People who do not vote can get a fine."},{"start":138.56,"end":141.56,"text":"A fine is money you pay when you break a rule."},{"start":142.1,"end":144.54,"text":"Because of this law, almost everyone votes."},{"start":145.38,"end":149.62,"text":"In 2025, 90.7% of enrolled voters voted."},{"start":150.52,"end":153.98,"text":"Enrolled voters are the people whose names are on the list of voters."},{"start":153.98,"end":158.44,"text":"Elections are on Saturdays, and people often vote in schools."},{"start":159.3,"end":163.18,"text":"Millions of people come on the day, so school parents cook for the long lines."},{"start":163.66,"end":164.98,"text":"The money helps the school."},{"start":165.7,"end":168.18,"text":"Australians call this a democracy sausage."},{"start":168.96,"end":171.88,"text":"In a democracy, people choose their leaders by voting."},{"start":173.38,"end":176.34,"text":"The Melbourne Cup is the most famous horse race in Australia."},{"start":177.34,"end":180.3,"text":"In a race, horses run to see who is fastest."},{"start":181.08,"end":183.4,"text":"People call this one the race that stops a nation."},{"start":184.12,"end":187.04,"text":"For a few minutes, many Australians stop to watch."},{"start":188.08,"end":192.38,"text":"When: the first Tuesday in November, at 3 pm."},{"start":192.38,"end":195.14,"text":"Where: Flemington Racecourse in Melbourne."},{"start":195.82,"end":198.94,"text":"How far: 3,200 metres."},{"start":198.94,"end":200.88,"text":"Why do so many people stop for one race?"},{"start":200.88,"end":205.06,"text":"Cup Day is a public holiday in Victoria, the state where Melbourne is."},{"start":205.86,"end":207.38,"text":"People there do not go to work."},{"start":207.96,"end":210.92,"text":"They go to the race, or they watch it on TV with friends."},{"start":211.94,"end":215.12,"text":"In other states, Cup Day is a normal work day."},{"start":215.44,"end":217.96,"text":"But many offices stop at 3 pm."},{"start":217.96,"end":220.12,"text":"People watch the race together on TV."},{"start":220.66,"end":222.52,"text":"Many offices also have a sweep."},{"start":222.52,"end":224.7,"text":"It is a small game for the race."},{"start":225.34,"end":227.38,"text":"Everyone pays the same, often a few dollars."},{"start":228.08,"end":230.1,"text":"Each person takes a horse's name from a hat."},{"start":230.7,"end":233.4,"text":"The person with the winning horse gets about half of the money."},{"start":234.04,"end":235.6,"text":"You do not need to know about horses."},{"start":236.3,"end":240.16,"text":"It is all luck, so everyone in the sweep has a horse to cheer for."},{"start":241.44,"end":244.76,"text":"In 2026, a horse called Point Of Law won."},{"start":245.48,"end":247.7,"text":"Its trainer was Ciaron Maher."},{"start":247.7,"end":249.94,"text":"A trainer gets a horse ready for races."},{"start":249.94,"end":253.88,"text":"Ciaron Maher also trained the horses in second and third place."},{"start":254.78,"end":257.88,"text":"This was the first time in 166 races."},{"start":258.7,"end":260.62,"text":"One trainer had the first three horses."},{"start":261.96,"end":262.4,"text":"No tips."},{"start":263.06,"end":266.54,"text":"In cafés and restaurants, people do not usually leave a tip."},{"start":267.28,"end":269.96,"text":"A tip is a little money for the person who serves you."},{"start":270.54,"end":270.8,"text":"Why?"},{"start":271.34,"end":273.34,"text":"Australian workers already get high pay."},{"start":273.76,"end":276.02,"text":"So they do not need tips to make enough money."},{"start":276.44,"end":279.6,"text":"The lowest pay the law allows is called the minimum wage."},{"start":280.34,"end":285.32,"text":"From 1 July 2026, it is $26.44 an hour."},{"start":285.8,"end":288.82,"text":"It is for most workers aged 21 or older."},{"start":288.82,"end":291.18,"text":"Super."},{"start":291.18,"end":296.66,"text":"From 1 July 2025, bosses must pay extra money for almost every worker."},{"start":297.42,"end":300.98,"text":"They must pay 12% of a worker's pay into a super fund."},{"start":301.88,"end":304.14,"text":"Super is short for superannuation."},{"start":304.72,"end":307.3,"text":"The fund keeps this money until you are old."},{"start":307.92,"end":308.12,"text":"Why?"},{"start":308.8,"end":311.32,"text":"So people have their own money when they stop work."},{"start":312.26,"end":313.9,"text":"This year there is a new rule."},{"start":314.56,"end":318.92,"text":"Now the boss pays super with every payday, the day you get your pay."},{"start":318.92,"end":321.58,"text":"Long service leave."},{"start":322.56,"end":326.32,"text":"After 10 years with the same company, workers get long service leave."},{"start":326.86,"end":329.34,"text":"It is a long holiday, and you still get your pay."},{"start":329.98,"end":333.54,"text":"In New South Wales, the state where Sydney is, it is two months."},{"start":334.48,"end":335.96,"text":"Other states have different rules."},{"start":336.64,"end":336.82,"text":"Why?"},{"start":337.52,"end":340.9,"text":"It is a thank-you for staying with one company for a long time."}],"words":[{"text":"Canberra","start":0,"end":0.46},{"text":"is","start":0.46,"end":0.88},{"text":"the","start":0.88,"end":1.06},{"text":"capital","start":1.06,"end":1.38},{"text":"of","start":1.38,"end":1.58},{"text":"Australia","start":1.58,"end":1.98},{"text":"and","start":2.56,"end":2.86},{"text":"it","start":2.86,"end":3.06},{"text":"is","start":3.06,"end":3.24},{"text":"a","start":3.24,"end":3.4},{"text":"planned","start":3.4,"end":3.72},{"text":"city","start":3.72,"end":4.12},{"text":"People","start":5.02,"end":5.18},{"text":"drew","start":5.18,"end":5.42},{"text":"the","start":5.42,"end":5.6},{"text":"city","start":5.6,"end":5.8},{"text":"on","start":5.8,"end":6.02},{"text":"paper","start":6.02,"end":6.3},{"text":"first","start":6.3,"end":6.76},{"text":"and","start":7.14,"end":7.38},{"text":"then","start":7.38,"end":7.6},{"text":"they","start":7.6,"end":7.78},{"text":"built","start":7.78,"end":7.96},{"text":"it","start":7.96,"end":8.36},{"text":"Why","start":8.98,"end":9.2},{"text":"When","start":10.3,"end":10.4},{"text":"Australia","start":10.4,"end":10.8},{"text":"became","start":10.8,"end":11.2},{"text":"one","start":11.2,"end":11.58},{"text":"country","start":11.58,"end":12.06},{"text":"Sydney","start":12.5,"end":12.62},{"text":"and","start":12.62,"end":12.88},{"text":"Melbourne","start":12.88,"end":13.2},{"text":"both","start":13.2,"end":13.6},{"text":"wante